#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:177
msgid "A floating label sits inside the empty field like a placeholder and moves to the top edge, smaller, as soon as the field is focused or filled. The plugin rebuilds the markup Contact Form 7 renders and ships the stylesheet; it needs no JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:178
msgid "Text, email, URL, telephone, number and textarea fields get floating labels. Checkboxes, radio buttons, selects, file uploads, quizzes and CAPTCHAs keep their original markup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:179
msgid "The label text comes from the form template (a <label> that encloses the field or points at its id) or from the placeholder option of the form-tag. A label in the template wins over a placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:180
msgid "Fields the plugin does not recognise are left exactly as Contact Form 7 renders them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-jgor-flcf7-admin.php:189
msgid "The settings of this screen apply to every form. Override them per form, per placement or per field; later layers win."
msgstr ""

